> Explain why deterministic validation matters when optimizing a GPU inference kernel.
# Why Deterministic Validation Matters for GPU Inference Kernels

When optimizing GPU kernels, determinism in validation isn't just a nice-to-have—it's foundational to producing trustworthy results. Here's why it matters:

## 1. Isolating Correctness from Performance

GPU optimizations introduce many sources of non-determinism:
- **Floating-point reordering** — FMA contraction, different reduction orders, and parallel reduction trees change summation order, producing slightly different results
- **Non-deterministic atomics** — concurrent updates to shared memory create order-dependent outcomes
- **Warp-level divergence** — different thread execution

